# Connection Details Template (Local Only)

Copy this file to `desk/config/connections.md` and fill in local values. The real
`connections.md` holds machine addresses, channel IDs, connected external accounts
and other local operator details.

**Decide where it lives, and say so at the top of your copy.** In the discoverer's
practice it is **tracked on the private remote and denied to the public one** — the
Two Chronicles pattern — because a Spirit that cannot read it cannot reach anything.
It was gitignored until 2026-08-07, and this template went on saying so for
eighteen days; a Spirit reading the stale word would helpfully un-stage a file the
practice depends on. If yours is gitignored instead, that is a fine choice, but it
must be written here rather than assumed.

## Purpose

This file is a local bridge card for Spirit-in-Cursor/Anvil. It answers: "From
this workstation, how do I reach Turtle and the relevant practice surfaces?"

It is not Turtle's runtime source of truth. Runtime topology belongs in
`~/turtleos/mage_registry.yaml`.

## Configuration Precedence

1. `~/turtleos/mage_registry.yaml` — canonical Turtle runtime topology.
2. `system/config/connections.md` — local operator reference for this workstation.
3. `TURTLE_SPEC.md` and lore — public pattern, with no secrets.

